--- import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro"; import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro"; import "../../styles/standards-poster.css"; import "../../styles/extended.css"; import metadata from "../../data/standards/japangaap/practical-solutions-overview.json"; --- <StandardPageLayout code={metadata.code} standardType={metadata.framework} title={metadata.title} description={metadata.description} issued={metadata.issued} latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment} status={metadata.status} summary={metadata.summary} bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice} > <Fragment slot="toc"> <PageToc items={[{"id":"s1","label":"Conceptual Framework Linkage"},{"id":"s2","label":"Scope — Where Practical Solutions Sit Within ASBJ's Output"},{"id":"s3","label":"Why a Faster, Narrower Document Type Exists"},{"id":"s4","label":"Status — Real Practical Force, Without Full Statement-Level Weight"},{"id":"s5","label":"Typical Trigger — New Laws, New Instruments, Urgent Questions"},{"id":"s6","label":"Illustrative Examples Across This Poster Series"},{"id":"s7","label":"The Eventual Path to Full Statement Status"},{"id":"s8","label":"Worked Example — a New Instrument Triggering a Practical Solution"},{"id":"s9","label":"Worked Example — Formalisation Into a Full Standard"},{"id":"s10","label":"Disclosure Requirements"},{"id":"s11","label":"Critical Judgments"},{"id":"s12","label":"Relationship to IAS/IFRS"},{"id":"s13","label":"Statement Mapping"},{"id":"s14","label":"Related Standards"},{"id":"s15","label":"Glossary"}]} /> </Fragment> <div class="wrap"> <div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Timely guidance for narrow, often urgent practical questions</div><div class="principle">"PRACTICAL SOLUTIONS" (実務対応報告) are a DISTINCT ASBJ document TYPE — separate from the FULL "ACCOUNTING STANDARDS" (ASBJ Statements) that form the CORE of J-GAAP. Where a full Accounting Standard addresses a BROAD topic through a comprehensive, multi-year due-process CYCLE, a Practical Solution addresses a NARROWER, often more URGENT practical question — frequently arising from a NEWLY introduced law, a NEW type of financial instrument, or an emerging accounting QUESTION not yet anticipated by the existing standards.</div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope — Where Practical Solutions Sit Within ASBJ's Output</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">One of several parallel ASBJ document types</div><div class="principle">As NOTED in the companion ASBJ Guidance No. 32 poster, ASBJ's output SPANS several PARALLEL document types — ACCOUNTING STANDARDS (Statements), IMPLEMENTATION GUIDANCE, TRANSFERRED GUIDANCE (older interpretive material carried FORWARD from a predecessor body), and PRACTICAL SOLUTIONS — EACH with its OWN numbering sequence and ROLE within the overall J-GAAP framework.</div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Why a Faster, Narrower Document Type Exists</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Bridging the gap between "no guidance" and "a full multi-year project"</div><div class="text-supporting">A FULL Accounting Standard project can take YEARS — appropriate for BROAD, foundational topics, but genuinely ILL-SUITED to a NARROW, URGENT practical question (e.g. how should a BRAND-NEW type of tax, or a NEWLY common financial instrument, be accounted for RIGHT NOW?). Practical Solutions FILL this gap — providing companies with TIMELY, AUTHORITATIVE guidance MUCH faster than the full Statement-level due-process CYCLE would allow.</div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Status — Real Practical Force, Without Full Statement-Level Weight</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Authoritative guidance, sometimes explicitly tentative</div><div class="text-supporting">A Practical Solution CARRIES genuine, AUTHORITATIVE practical force — companies are EXPECTED to follow its guidance — but it does NOT carry the SAME formal, comprehensive due-process WEIGHT as a full ASBJ Statement. Some Practical Solutions are EXPLICITLY labelled "TENTATIVE" (as with the companion Special Corporate Tax for Defense poster), SIGNALLING that FURTHER refinement — or eventual FORMALISATION into a full Statement — may FOLLOW.</div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Typical Trigger — New Laws, New Instruments, Urgent Questions</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">The recurring pattern behind most Practical Solutions</div><div class="td-table"><div class="th cols-12-18"><span>Trigger type</span><span>Example (illustrative)</span></div> <div class="tr cols-12-18"><span>New tax legislation</span><span>The Special Corporate Tax for Defense (2026); the OECD global minimum tax rules</span></div> <div class="tr cols-12-18"><span>New financial instruments/practices</span><span>Virtual currency accounting; LIBOR transition hedge accounting relief</span></div> <div class="tr cols-12-18"><span>Narrow entity types</span><span>Trust accounting; deferred asset treatment for specific arrangements</span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Illustrative Examples Across This Poster Series</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Practical Solutions already encountered in this series</div><div class="text-supporting">This poster series has ALREADY covered ONE concrete example — the Practical Solution on the TENTATIVE Treatment of Accounting for and Disclosures of Special Corporate Tax for Defense (issued February 27, 2026) — ILLUSTRATING the general PATTERN: a narrow, urgent, tax-law-driven question addressed QUICKLY, OUTSIDE the full Statement-level cycle.</div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>The Eventual Path to Full Statement Status</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Some Practical Solutions eventually get absorbed into a full Statement</div><div class="text-supporting">AS discussed in the companion ASBJ Statement No. 27 (Revised 2026) poster, a TENTATIVE Practical Solution addressing a genuinely SIGNIFICANT, LASTING accounting question may EVENTUALLY be FORMALISED into a full ASBJ Statement — once the underlying practice has MATURED and the ASBJ judges the topic WARRANTS the fuller, more COMPREHENSIVE due-process treatment.</div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Worked Example — a New Instrument Triggering a Practical Solution</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Timely guidance for an emerging accounting question</div> <div class="worked"><div class="wk-title">Example: A new type of digital asset emerging in the market</div><div class="wk-body">A genuinely new type of financial instrument or digital asset becomes common in the Japanese market, without existing J-GAAP standards clearly addressing its treatment.</div><div class="wk-answer">RATHER than waiting for a FULL, multi-year Accounting Standard project, the ASBJ may issue a PRACTICAL SOLUTION addressing the SPECIFIC recognition, measurement, and disclosure QUESTIONS this new instrument raises — giving preparers TIMELY, authoritative guidance MUCH sooner than a full Statement-level project would allow.</div></div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example — Formalisation Into a Full Standard</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Graduating from tentative guidance to permanent standard</div> <div class="worked"><div class="wk-title">Example: A tentative tax measure becoming a lasting fixture</div><div class="wk-body">A tentative Practical Solution addressing a new tax measure remains in place for several years, with the underlying tax practice becoming well-established and stable.</div><div class="wk-answer">The ASBJ may EVENTUALLY fold the Practical Solution's SUBSTANCE into a FULL Accounting Standard (e.g. an amendment to the relevant tax accounting Statement) — REPRESENTING the NATURAL "graduation" path from FAST, tentative interim guidance TOWARD permanent, comprehensive Statement-level treatment.</div></div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What a typical Practical Solution requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>The nature of the specific practical question being addressed</span><span>Any tentative status, and the basis for the interim treatment prescribed</span></div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Critical Judgments</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div> <div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Whether a specific fact pattern falls within a narrowly-scoped Practical Solution's coverage</span></div></div> <div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Varies by the specific Practical Solution's subject matter</span></div></div></div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Relationship to IAS/IFRS</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">A rough parallel to IFRIC Interpretations and narrow-scope amendments</div><div class="text-supporting">Internationally, the IFRS Interpretations Committee (IFRIC) and the IASB's OWN narrow-scope amendments serve a BROADLY SIMILAR function — addressing SPECIFIC, often URGENT application questions MORE QUICKLY than a full new IFRS Standard project would allow. J-GAAP's Practical Solutions occupy a ROUGHLY analogous ROLE within the J-GAAP hierarchy, though the SPECIFIC procedural mechanics and formal STATUS differ between the two systems.</div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Varies by specific Practical Solution</div><div class="td-table"><div class="th cols-16-1-14"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div> <div class="tr cols-16-1-14"><span>Varies</span><span>Varies</span><span>Depends entirely on the specific Practical Solution's subject matter</span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div><div class="td-table"><div class="th cols-08-2"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div> <div class="tr cols-08-2"><span>Practical Solution on Special Corporate Tax for Defense</span><span>A concrete example of this document type covered elsewhere in this poster series</span></div> <div class="tr cols-08-2"><span>ASBJ Guidance No. 32</span><span>Illustrates ASBJ's broader parallel numbering systems across document types</span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cn span2"> <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Practical Solution (実務対応報告)</div><div class="glossary-def">A narrower, more quickly issued ASBJ document type addressing specific, often urgent practical accounting questions, frequently arising from new laws or instruments.</div></div> <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Transferred Guidance</div><div class="glossary-def">Older interpretive material carried forward from a predecessor standard-setting body, forming another of ASBJ's parallel document types.</div></div> </div> </div><div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Japan GAAP terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><span class="litem"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (貸借対照表)</span><span class="litem"><span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span> Statement of Income / Profit and Loss Statement (損益計算書)</span><span class="litem"><span class="badge bo">Net Assets</span> 純資産の部</span><span class="litem"><span class="badge be">SCNA</span> Statement of Changes in Net Assets (株主資本等変動計算書)</span><span class="litem"><span class="badge bc">SCF</span> Statement of Cash Flows (キャッシュ・フロー計算書)</span></div></div> </div> </StandardPageLayout> 